  "description": "Write Bevy games in C#. Mark a struct [Behavior], give it [OnUpdate] methods, and a\n            source generator registers it with the Bevy schedule as both a component and a system.\n            Bevy is the engine underneath, providing its ECS, scheduler, renderer and input\n            through a native bridge.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "BevyCSharp",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-12T23:31:33.25Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MPL-2.0",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MPL-2.0",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "ekpZeLfEPhTd6jYVCdsYVuZkIDVdXN8zdrpcl/lkdvH1JVUd22lHdMv3SaqtELQ0olU6uggc4WelKP2AiDgTbw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 227075572,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/EggyStudio/BevyCSharp",
  "published": "2026-11-12T23:14:59.277Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The pack strips the Linux and macOS bridges and keeps each full library with its build id as an artifact by version, and a crash file writes each frame as the bridge's build id and an offset, which build/name-crash.py names from it.\nThe comments say what the code is as it stands, telling no earlier form, mend or fault and naming no program built on the library as their example, and STYLE.md's checks carry the search that finds them.\nThe screen's probes, the glow texels and the light pass take their points of the depth as ways from the eye and add the eye where the field, the probes or a light are read, which moves no reading measured.\nA pixel on the picture's edge takes its step from the neighbor inside, where the clamped one gave a step of nothing whose facing turned with the rounding, and the GI tests count their traced frames from the frame every pipeline is ready.\nA pass takes a pixel's point and its way into the sky from the eye in the view's own numbers, so the night sky 4,450 units from the origin draws its stars as at it, and the rain's streaks and splashes are placed by their corners from the eye.\nA glow texel looks its history up less the quarter texel its point stands off its middle, so a still view keeps the glow light's light over 32 frames and holds still where it kept a frame's and a seventh.\nThe animated picture's reader moves to Rendering and the field curve to Animation, which closes Animation's opening to the command line, and N 1.6 holds each remaining opening to build/norm/1.6.txt, where each says why and what the compiler finds it reaches.\nThe tests' Assets folder moves to the areas, each of 146 files whole to the folder of the area it tests, and the asset server's twelve stay.",
